- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests`

**How to implement.** One window per kit: choosing a kit whose window is open brings that window forward instead of opening the kit again (001 §E 'Concurrency: one window per kit'; the S5.3 brief: opening a kit that is already open activates its window). The windows meet in the host-layer registry that already keeps Materials and Library single-instance (`WindowLauncher.fs:108`, `WindowRegistry`; `WindowLauncher.fs:191`, `WindowLauncher.create`), keyed by the kit's canonical folder (step 181); no second registry is written. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: `WindowKey` (`WindowLauncher.fs:34`) gains `KitWindowKey of KitFolder`, documented in one line: a constructor window, keyed by its kit's canonical folder. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `KitWindowPresence` = `KitWindowActivated` (a window held the kit and was brought forward) | `NoKitWindowOpen` (no window holds it). `type KitFolder with member this.windowKey : WindowLauncher.WindowKey` is `KitWindowKey this.canonical`, and `member this.activateKitWindow () : KitWindowPresence` calls `openOrActivate this.windowKey` of `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory that answers `WindowNotRegisteredErr` of its key (`WindowLauncher.fs:66`), `SelectWindowModality.defaultValue` and `BrowseOpen`: `Ok (ActivatedWindow _)` is `KitWindowActivated`, and every other answer is `NoKitWindowOpen`, because that factory never builds a window. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs` (steps 176, 177): `KitStartContext` gains `activateKitWindow : KitFolder -> KitWindowPresence` after `showKit`, documented in one line. In `updateKitStart`, `CreateKit folder`, `OpenKit folder` and `OpenKitReadOnly folder` first call `m.context.activateKitWindow folder`: `KitWindowActivated` answers the model with no offer and no status, and opens, bumps and hands over nothing, because the kit's window holds it and its history entry was bumped when that window opened; `NoKitWindowOpen` runs step 177's open unchanged. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179) composes `activateKitWindow = fun folder -> match folder.activateKitWindow () with KitWindowActivated -> this.Close (); KitWindowActivated | NoKitWindowOpen -> NoKitWindowOpen`, so the screen closes when it brought a kit's window forward, as it closes when it hands a kit over. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `rootWindowFactory` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:44`), exhaustive over `WindowKey`, answers `KitWindowKey _` with `Error (WindowFactoryFailedErr (key, "a kit window opens over its opened kit"))`, because a constructor window is built by the kit hand-off (step 191), never by the root factory; its doc says so in no more words. (6) Tests. `KitStartTests`' fixture context (step 176) and `KitStartWindowTests`' contexts (step 178) pass `activateKitWindow = fun _ -> NoKitWindowOpen`, and every earlier fact keeps its assertions. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs` gains `a kit whose window is open is activated, not opened, bumped or handed over`: over a kit made by `openKitAt` and closed, and a context whose `activateKitWindow` answers `KitWindowActivated` for that folder and records each call, `OpenKit`, `CreateKit` and `OpenKitReadOnly` of the folder each record one activation and no shown kit, answer no offer and no status, leave the history unchanged and leave the folder without `.oc/lock`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs` gains `two spellings of one kit folder are one window key, and no window holds a new kit`: the `windowKey`s of `C:/kits/a` and of the same folder written with backslashes, a trailing one and in upper case are equal, and `activateKitWindow ()` of a GUID-named folder under the test output answers `NoKitWindowOpen`.

**Acceptance.** After the registry key lands, `KitFolder.activateKitWindow` MUST bring forward a window registered under the kit's canonical folder and answer `NoKitWindowOpen` otherwise, and the start screen's open messages MUST activate such a window instead of opening the kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit whose window is open is activated, not opened, bumped or handed over` and `two spellings of one kit folder are one window key, and no window holds a new kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
